### Method reminder

Define e-learning as learning delivered by electronic means, then link each advantage to the student's situation.

### Solution

**(a)** E-learning is learning in which the teaching materials and activities are delivered and followed through electronic devices and networks (computer, tablet, phone, Internet, learning platform).

**(b)** Any two:

- the student can access lessons, videos and exercises without travelling to a distant school;
- the student can learn at the time and pace that suit him or her;
- the student can reach teachers and resources better than those available locally;
- materials can be reused and revised as often as needed.
